  "notes": "{更迭|こうてつ} means to replace or remove someone from an official position, often used in political and business contexts.\n\nWRITING:\n- {更|こう} (change, renew)\n- {迭|てつ} (alternate, replace)\n\nUSAGE:\n- {更迭|こうてつ}する (to replace/remove - suru verb)\n- {更迭|こうてつ}される (to be replaced/removed)\n- 〜を{更迭|こうてつ}する (to remove ~ from position)\n- {大臣|だいじん}の{更迭|こうてつ} (cabinet reshuffle)\n- {監督|かんとく}の{更迭|こうてつ} (manager replacement in sports)\n- {幹部|かんぶ}の{更迭|こうてつ} (executive reshuffle)\n- Often implies removal due to failure, scandal, or pressure\n- More formal than {交代|こうたい} (replacement/rotation)\n- Common in news reporting\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {解任|かいにん} (dismissal)\n- {辞任|じにん} (resignation)\n- {交代|こうたい} (replacement - neutral term)",
